    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d835">

                <pb facs="0932" n="738" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg738"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">871.6363/7–1745: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 835<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kennan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of State</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d835-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-17T16:00:00+03:00">July 17, 1945—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2597. By letter to Vyshinski of July 11,
                    British Ambassador<anchor n="2" xml:id="d835-f2"/> stated British Government
                    could not accept Soviet Government <pb facs="0933" n="739" xml:id="pg739"/>
                    views expressed in February 26 Foreign Office note on removal oil field
                    equipment from Rumania. (To Dept, repeated
                    Bucharest 91, London 368) Clark Kerr
                    protested continued Soviet requisitioning and removal British equipment.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Kennan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d835-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d835-f1-content">
                <p>The gist of this message was included in telegram No. 65 of July 19 from
                        Grew to Byrnes (file No. 800.00 Summaries/7–1945).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d835-f2" n="2" xml:id="d835-f2-content">
                <p>Sir Archibald Clark Kerr.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
